# Exception: this is game content (debug-only launch stages/scripts), not
# a CMake Debug/Release build-output directory - the **/debug/ rule above
# is aimed at the latter and would otherwise also catch this real,
# tracked source folder. Updated 2026-08-28 twice the same day - first
# when resources/scripts/ moved to src/, then again minutes later when
# games/caravellius/ itself moved to caravellius/ (repo root) - the
# negation is keyed to the literal path, so each move silently stopped it
# matching anything, with no warning (git just quietly stops tracking new
# content under debug/ - confirmed live both times via `git ls-files`
# coming back empty for the directory right after each rename). Any
# future rename of a directory on this path needs this same follow-up.
!caravellius/src/debug/
!caravellius/src/debug/**
**/Release/
**/release/
**/GeneratedFiles/
**/Build/
**/build/
**/CMakeFiles/
**/out/
**/_deps/

# Local, per-developer VSCode config - the tracked source of truth lives in
# docs/vscode/.vscode (see docs/vscode/README.md); copy from there instead
# of editing here directly, so intentional changes don't get lost.
/.vscode/
